# Copy to `/root/selvage-compose/.env` and fill in. Compose reads this file from
# the project directory, which is the directory the compose file is in, so
# nothing has to be exported and no shell has to have run.
#
# These are the Pi's *intent*: which published images the next
# `docker compose up -d` will run. They are separate from `compose.yaml` because
# they change on a release and the shape does not.
#
# **Digests, not tags**, and the values below are real digests rather than
# placeholders: a tag is a name the publisher can repoint, so a copy of this
# file deployed unchanged would run content nobody reviewed, and `${VAR:?…}` in
# the compose file only catches an empty value. A stale digest fails loudly at
# `docker pull`, which is the right way round. Move both on every release —
# README.md has the command that resolves a tag to its index digest through the
# registry's anonymous pull flow.
#
# Both are the releases the Pi runs today, which are the ones the public demo
# runs too: one page release, one server release, read off the registry rather
# than copied from the other file.
#
# The page inside the `selvaged` image is not the one a visitor here gets: the
# Dockerfile bakes the `web_client` revision it pins, the Pi's compose turns that
# page off, and `SELVAGE_WEB_IMAGE` is what answers `/`.

# selvaged 0.2.1 (ghcr.io/selvage-protocol/selvaged:0.2.1). FSL-1.1-MIT.
SELVAGED_IMAGE=ghcr.io/selvage-protocol/selvaged@sha256:87e13601f5b491fd9a4957237d037893cb78d7feeffd394682e370b3c32a35fe

# selvage-web 0.3.1 (ghcr.io/selvage-protocol/selvage-web:0.3.1). MIT OR Apache-2.0.
SELVAGE_WEB_IMAGE=ghcr.io/selvage-protocol/selvage-web@sha256:9d32eee715e1d57018956ebaba1c79b2366130074948396a63cf3f90eefa775c
